Applies on top of tools/kmc-as-lw-dest-temp.patch (decompals/mips-binutils-2.6 + tools/no-float-doubleword.patch +
tools/kmc-as-fixes.patch). Two nop rules of the assembler that built the ROM's libultra objects, both only under
--fp-move-nops (the libultra pieces src/18020_C5030.c .. src/18020_D30C0.c; every game unit assembles byte-identical):

  1. Two hazard nops between an FP compare and the filled branch right after it. GCC writes the compare, then
     `.set noreorder; bc1f L; <slot>`; the game units' assembler pads one nop (kmc_cc_pending, at the branch), the
     libultra assembler padded two: `c.le.d; nop; nop; bc1tl; sub.d` (25 sites in the ROM, never one). That is
     stock gas's nop at the `.set noreorder` (mips_emit_delays, which tools/kmc-as-fixes.patch switched off for the
     game units) on top of the KMC one. A compare two instructions back keeps its single nop (`c.le.d; addiu; nop;
     bc1t`, 11 sites), and the reorder-mode unfilled branch keeps its single nop (`c.lt.s; nop; bc1t; nop`, 18
     sites). Counted 2026-11-06 with `objdump -d -z` (without -z objdump folds two nops into `...`, which is how
     a first version of this patch misread the ROM as having none). tc-mips.c mips_emit_delays.

  2. The VR4300 mulmul text fix treats a line that starts in column 0 as a float multiply: a label line or an
     empty line (gas/input-file.c, `local_28 == cur_insn`, which the fixes patch removed for the game units). So a
     mul or dmul of any width right after a label, or right after the empty line GCC leaves behind every `.set
     reorder`, gets a nop in front of it: `.L28: nop; mul.d`, `.L509: nop; mult t2,t6`, `bnez; cvt.d.s; nop;
     mul.d` (13 sites in the ROM: 12 at branch targets, 1 after a filled slot; none without the nop).

The library functions that AGENTS.md listed as "one nop short, not the C" are these two rules:
func_801C4040, func_801C48A0, func_801C5810, func_801C59C0, func_801C9C20, func_801C9D24, func_801CAFC8,
func_801CC050, func_801CE300, func_801CF0C0, func_801D3020 (rule 1), func_801C6000, func_801C7EB0, func_801C7F54,
func_801CA844, func_801CC118 (rule 2; func_801CC118 also has a real code difference at +0x760). func_801C7110 is
relocation annotations (D_80000004/08/0C), func_801C4030 is `jr ra; sqrt.s` in the slot, hand-written: neither is
this patch.

Re-apply with: git apply --ignore-whitespace tools/kmc-as-libultra-nops.patch (after the three above).
Build and verify: tools/kmc-as-build.sh (configure + make as in tools/kmc-as-fixes.patch, then
tools/fable/as_verify.py old new: objdiff-cli judges every unit against expected/, game units must be identical).

